%%report facility-by-state title: FACILITies by state entity: FACILITY chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Facility record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How facilities divide across state, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(state::text, '(unset)') AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_facility WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report facility-by-facility-type title: FACILITies by facility type entity: FACILITY chart: pie x: facility_type y: records help: Operational Facility record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How facilities divide across facility type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(facility_type::text, '(unset)') AS facility_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_facility WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report facility-by-country-code title: FACILITies by country code entity: FACILITY chart: pie x: country_code y: records help: Operational Facility record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How facilities divide across country code, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(country_code::text, '(unset)') AS country_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_facility WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report department-by-department-type title: DEPARTMENTs by department type entity: DEPARTMENT chart: bar x: department_type y: records help: Operational Department record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How departments divide across department type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(department_type::text, '(unset)') AS department_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_department WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report department-top-department-name title: DEPARTMENTs: the most common department name entity: DEPARTMENT chart: bar x: department_name y: records help: Operational Department record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The ten most frequent values of department name among departments; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(department_name, '(blank)') AS department_name, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_department WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report department-top-location-wing title: DEPARTMENTs: the most common location wing entity: DEPARTMENT chart: bar x: location_wing y: records help: Operational Department record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The ten most frequent values of location wing among departments; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(location_wing, '(blank)') AS location_wing, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_department WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report employee-by-status title: EMPLOYEEs by status entity: EMPLOYEE chart: pie x: status y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employees divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-by-employment-type title: EMPLOYEEs by employment type entity: EMPLOYEE chart: pie x: employment_type y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employees divide across employment type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(employment_type::text, '(unset)') AS employment_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-by-gender title: EMPLOYEEs by gender entity: EMPLOYEE chart: pie x: gender y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employees divide across gender, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(gender::text, '(unset)') AS gender, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-lifecycle title: EMPLOYEE lifecycle entity: EMPLOYEE chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where employees sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'DRAFT' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ACTIVE', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'ON_LEAVE', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'SUSPENDED', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'NOTICE_PERIOD', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'SEPARATED', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report employee-created-per-month title: EMPLOYEEs created per month entity: EMPLOYEE chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New employees per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-join-date-per-month title: EMPLOYEEs by join date entity: EMPLOYEE chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. EMPLOYEEs grouped by the month of join date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', join_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND join_date IS NOT NULL AND join_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND join_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-end-date-per-month title: EMPLOYEEs by end date entity: EMPLOYEE chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. EMPLOYEEs grouped by the month of end date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', end_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND end_date IS NOT NULL AND end_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND end_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-date-of-birth-per-month title: EMPLOYEEs by date of birth entity: EMPLOYEE chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. EMPLOYEEs grouped by the month of date of birth, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', date_of_birth), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND date_of_birth IS NOT NULL AND date_of_birth >= now() - interval '24 months' AND date_of_birth < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-per-employee title: EMPLOYEEs per employee entity: EMPLOYEE chart: bar x: employee y: records help: Operational Employee record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which employee the most employees belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.employee_number::text, '(none)') AS employee, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee x LEFT JOIN bus_employee p ON p.id = x.employee_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report employee-payroll-profile-by-payment-method title: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILEs by payment method entity: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILE chart: pie x: payment_method y: records help: Operational Employee Payroll Profile record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employee_payroll_profiles divide across payment method, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(payment_method::text, '(unset)') AS payment_method, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_payroll_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-payroll-profile-created-per-month title: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILEs created per month entity: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILE chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Employee Payroll Profile record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New employee_payroll_profiles per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_payroll_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-payroll-profile-per-employee-payroll-profile title: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILEs per employee payroll profile entity: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILE chart: bar x: employee_payroll_profile y: records help: Operational Employee Payroll Profile record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which employee payroll profile the most employee_payroll_profiles belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.tax_identifier::text, '(none)') AS employee_payroll_profile, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_payroll_profile x LEFT JOIN bus_employee_payroll_profile p ON p.id = x.employee_payroll_profile_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report employee-payroll-profile-per-employee title: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILEs per employee entity: EMPLOYEE_PAYROLL_PROFILE chart: bar x: employee y: records help: Operational Employee Payroll Profile record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which employee the most employee_payroll_profiles belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.employee_number::text, '(none)') AS employee, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_payroll_profile x LEFT JOIN bus_employee p ON p.id = x.employee_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report doctor-by-doctor-type title: DOCTORs by doctor type entity: DOCTOR chart: pie x: doctor_type y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How doctors divide across doctor type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(doctor_type::text, '(unset)') AS doctor_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report doctor-created-per-month title: DOCTORs created per month entity: DOCTOR chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New doctors per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report doctor-created-by-weekday title: DOCTORs created by day of the week entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which days doctors are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report doctor-changed-per-month title: DOCTORs last changed per month entity: DOCTOR chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How recently doctors were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report doctor-age-bands title: How recently doctors were changed entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report doctor-edit-churn title: How often doctors are edited entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report doctor-removed-per-month title: DOCTORs removed per month entity: DOCTOR chart: line x: month y: removed help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records withdrawn from use each month; a rising line means the register is being cleared faster than it is kept. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', deleted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS removed FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report doctor-license-expiry-date-per-month title: DOCTORs by license expiry date entity: DOCTOR chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. DOCTORs grouped by the month of license expiry date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', license_expiry_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND license_expiry_date IS NOT NULL AND license_expiry_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND license_expiry_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report doctor-is-active-share title: DOCTORs: is active entity: DOCTOR chart: pie x: is_active y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The share of doctors where is active holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN is_active THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS is_active, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report doctor-per-doctor title: DOCTORs per doctor entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: doctor y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which doctor the most doctors belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.license_number::text, '(none)') AS doctor, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor x LEFT JOIN bus_doctor p ON p.id = x.doctor_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report doctor-per-employee title: DOCTORs per employee entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: employee y: records help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which employee the most doctors belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.employee_number::text, '(none)') AS employee, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_doctor x LEFT JOIN bus_employee p ON p.id = x.employee_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report doctor-completeness title: How complete doctors are entity: DOCTOR chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Operational Doctor record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. For each optional field, how many doctors leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'doctor' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE doctor_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'license expiry date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE license_expiry_date IS NULL) FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'qualification', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE qualification IS NULL) FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'contact email', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE contact_email IS NULL) FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'contact phone', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE contact_phone IS NULL) FROM bus_doctor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
