%%report user-account-by-primary-role title: USER_ACCOUNTs by primary role entity: USER_ACCOUNT chart: bar x: primary_role y: records help: Operational User Account record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How user_accounts divide across primary role, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(primary_role::text, '(unset)') AS primary_role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_user_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report user-account-lifecycle title: USER_ACCOUNT lifecycle entity: USER_ACCOUNT chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational User Account record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where user_accounts sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'PENDING_ACTIVATION' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ACTIVE', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'LOCKED', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'SUSPENDED', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'DISABLED', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_user_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
