%%report consent-per-consent title: CONSENTs per consent entity: CONSENT chart: bar x: consent y: records help: Operational Consent record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which consent the most consents belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.consent_reference::text, '(none)') AS consent, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_consent x LEFT JOIN bus_consent p ON p.id = x.consent_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report consent-per-patient title: CONSENTs per patient entity: CONSENT chart: bar x: patient y: records help: Operational Consent record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which patient the most consents belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.medical_record_number::text, '(none)') AS patient, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_consent x LEFT JOIN bus_patient p ON p.id = x.patient_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report consent-completeness title: How complete consents are entity: CONSENT chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Operational Consent record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. For each optional field, how many consents leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'consent' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE consent_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'recipient', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE recipient IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'effective at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE effective_at IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'expires at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE expires_at IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'withdrawn at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE withdrawn_at IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'document reference', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE document_reference IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'withdrawal reason', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE withdrawal_reason IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'active at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE active_at IS NULL) FROM bus_consent WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-by-status title: APPOINTMENTs by status entity: APPOINTMENT chart: bar x: status y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How appointments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-by-triage-priority title: APPOINTMENTs by triage priority entity: APPOINTMENT chart: pie x: triage_priority y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How appointments divide across triage priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(triage_priority::text, '(unset)') AS triage_priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-by-appointment-type title: APPOINTMENTs by appointment type entity: APPOINTMENT chart: pie x: appointment_type y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How appointments divide across appointment type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(appointment_type::text, '(unset)') AS appointment_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-by-channel title: APPOINTMENTs by channel entity: APPOINTMENT chart: pie x: channel y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How appointments divide across channel, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(channel::text, '(unset)') AS channel, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report appointment-lifecycle title: APPOINTMENT lifecycle entity: APPOINTMENT chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where appointments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'REQUESTED' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'SCHEDULED', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'CONFIRMED', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'CHECKED_IN', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'IN_CONSULTATION', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'COMPLETED', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'CANCELLED', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'NO_SHOW', 7 UNION ALL SELECT 'RESCHEDULED', 8) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report appointment-created-per-month title: APPOINTMENTs created per month entity: APPOINTMENT chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New appointments per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report appointment-created-by-weekday title: APPOINTMENTs created by day of the week entity: APPOINTMENT chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which days appointments are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report appointment-changed-per-month title: APPOINTMENTs last changed per month entity: APPOINTMENT chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How recently appointments were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report appointment-age-bands title: How recently appointments were changed entity: APPOINTMENT chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report appointment-edit-churn title: How often appointments are edited entity: APPOINTMENT chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report appointment-appointment-date-per-month title: APPOINTMENTs by appointment date entity: APPOINTMENT chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Appointment record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. APPOINTMENTs grouped by the month of appointment date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', appointment_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_appointment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND appointment_date IS NOT NULL AND appointment_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND appointment_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
