%%report ward-created-by-weekday title: WARDs created by day of the week entity: WARD chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which days wards are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report ward-changed-per-month title: WARDs last changed per month entity: WARD chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How recently wards were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report ward-age-bands title: How recently wards were changed entity: WARD chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report ward-isolation-capable-share title: WARDs: isolation capable entity: WARD chart: pie x: isolation_capable y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The share of wards where isolation capable holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN isolation_capable THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS isolation_capable, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report ward-is-active-share title: WARDs: is active entity: WARD chart: pie x: is_active y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The share of wards where is active holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN is_active THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS is_active, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report ward-licensed-capacity-by-ward-type title: Total licensed capacity by ward type entity: WARD chart: bar x: ward_type y: total_licensed_capacity help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. WARDs added up on licensed capacity, split by ward type, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(ward_type::text, '(unset)') AS ward_type, ROUND(SUM(licensed_capacity)::numeric, 2) AS total_licensed_capacity FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report ward-licensed-capacity-per-month title: Average licensed capacity per month entity: WARD chart: line x: month y: average_licensed_capacity help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The average licensed capacity of wards created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(licensed_capacity)::numeric, 2) AS average_licensed_capacity FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report ward-largest-by-licensed-capacity title: The ten largest wards by licensed capacity entity: WARD chart: bar x: record y: licensed_capacity help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The records with the highest licensed capacity; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, licensed_capacity FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND licensed_capacity IS NOT NULL ORDER BY licensed_capacity DESC LIMIT 10
%%report ward-per-ward title: WARDs per ward entity: WARD chart: bar x: ward y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which ward the most wards belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS ward, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward x LEFT JOIN bus_ward p ON p.id = x.ward_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report ward-licensed-capacity-per-ward title: Total licensed capacity per ward entity: WARD chart: bar x: ward y: total_licensed_capacity help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. WARDs added up on licensed capacity for each ward, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS ward, ROUND(SUM(x.licensed_capacity)::numeric, 2) AS total_licensed_capacity FROM bus_ward x LEFT JOIN bus_ward p ON p.id = x.ward_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report ward-top-location-description title: WARDs: the most common location description entity: WARD chart: bar x: location_description y: records help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The ten most frequent values of location description among wards; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(location_description, '(blank)') AS location_description, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report ward-completeness title: How complete wards are entity: WARD chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Operational Ward record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. For each optional field, how many wards leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'ward' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ward_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'nursing station phone', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE nursing_station_phone IS NULL) FROM bus_ward WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report bed-by-status title: BEDs by status entity: BED chart: pie x: status y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How beds divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report bed-by-bed-type title: BEDs by bed type entity: BED chart: bar x: bed_type y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How beds divide across bed type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(bed_type::text, '(unset)') AS bed_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report bed-lifecycle title: BED lifecycle entity: BED chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where beds sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'AVAILABLE' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'RESERVED', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'OCCUPIED', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'CLEANING', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'MAINTENANCE', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'BLOCKED', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report bed-created-per-month title: BEDs created per month entity: BED chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New beds per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report bed-created-by-weekday title: BEDs created by day of the week entity: BED chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which days beds are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report bed-age-bands title: How recently beds were changed entity: BED chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report bed-last-cleaned-at-per-month title: BEDs by last cleaned at entity: BED chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Bed record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. BEDs grouped by the month of last cleaned at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', last_cleaned_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_bed WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND last_cleaned_at IS NOT NULL AND last_cleaned_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND last_cleaned_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
