%%report claim-decision-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (CLAIM_DECISION) entity: CLAIM_DECISION chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: Operational Claim Decision record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. The average amount of claim_decisions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_claim_decision WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report employee-credential-by-status title: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIALs by status entity: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIAL chart: pie x: status y: records help: Operational Employee Credential record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employee_credentials divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_credential WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-credential-by-credential-type title: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIALs by credential type entity: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIAL chart: pie x: credential_type y: records help: Operational Employee Credential record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How employee_credentials divide across credential type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(credential_type::text, '(unset)') AS credential_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_credential WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report employee-credential-lifecycle title: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIAL lifecycle entity: EMPLOYEE_CREDENTIAL chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Employee Credential record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where employee_credentials sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'PENDING_VERIFICATION' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ACTIVE', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'EXPIRED', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'SUSPENDED', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'REVOKED', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_employee_credential WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
