%%report service-request-lifecycle title: SERVICE_REQUEST lifecycle entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where service_requests sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'OPEN' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ASSIGNED', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'IN_PROGRESS', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'COMPLETED', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'CANCELLED', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report service-request-created-per-month title: SERVICE_REQUESTs created per month entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New service_requests per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report service-request-assigned-at-per-month title: SERVICE_REQUESTs by assigned at entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. SERVICE_REQUESTs grouped by the month of assigned at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', assigned_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND assigned_at IS NOT NULL AND assigned_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND assigned_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report service-request-in-progress-at-per-month title: SERVICE_REQUESTs by in progress at entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. SERVICE_REQUESTs grouped by the month of in progress at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', in_progress_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND in_progress_at IS NOT NULL AND in_progress_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND in_progress_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report service-request-completed-at-per-month title: SERVICE_REQUESTs by completed at entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. SERVICE_REQUESTs grouped by the month of completed at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', completed_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND completed_at IS NOT NULL AND completed_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND completed_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report service-request-per-service-request title: SERVICE_REQUESTs per service request entity: SERVICE_REQUEST chart: bar x: service_request y: records help: Operational Service Request record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which service request the most service_requests belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.request_number::text, '(none)') AS service_request, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_request x LEFT JOIN bus_service_request p ON p.id = x.service_request_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
