%%report complaint-by-complaint-type title: COMPLAINTs by complaint type entity: COMPLAINT chart: pie x: complaint_type y: records help: Operational Complaint record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How complaints divide across complaint type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(complaint_type::text, '(unset)') AS complaint_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_complaint WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report complaint-lifecycle title: COMPLAINT lifecycle entity: COMPLAINT chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Complaint record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where complaints sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'OPEN' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ACKNOWLEDGED', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'INVESTIGATING', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'RESOLVED', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'CLOSED', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'REJECTED', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_complaint WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report complaint-created-per-month title: COMPLAINTs created per month entity: COMPLAINT chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Complaint record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New complaints per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_complaint WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report complaint-per-complaint title: COMPLAINTs per complaint entity: COMPLAINT chart: bar x: complaint y: records help: Operational Complaint record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which complaint the most complaints belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.complaint_number::text, '(none)') AS complaint, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_complaint x LEFT JOIN bus_complaint p ON p.id = x.complaint_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report housekeeping-task-by-status title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASKs by status entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: bar x: status y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How housekeeping_tasks divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report housekeeping-task-by-task-type title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASKs by task type entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: pie x: task_type y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. How housekeeping_tasks divide across task type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(task_type::text, '(unset)') AS task_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report housekeeping-task-lifecycle title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK lifecycle entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: bar x: state y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Where housekeeping_tasks sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'OPEN' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'ASSIGNED', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'IN_PROGRESS', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'INSPECTION', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'COMPLETED', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'REJECTED', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'CANCELLED', 6) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report housekeeping-task-created-per-month title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASKs created per month entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. New housekeeping_tasks per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report housekeeping-task-per-housekeeping-task title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASKs per housekeeping task entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: bar x: housekeeping_task y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which housekeeping task the most housekeeping_tasks belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.task_type::text, '(none)') AS housekeeping_task, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task x LEFT JOIN bus_housekeeping_task p ON p.id = x.housekeeping_task_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report housekeeping-task-per-service-request title: HOUSEKEEPING_TASKs per service request entity: HOUSEKEEPING_TASK chart: bar x: service_request y: records help: Operational Housekeeping Task record used by hospital staff from initial capture through accountable completion, preserving the evidence needed for care, administration and audit. Which service request the most housekeeping_tasks belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.request_number::text, '(none)') AS service_request, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_housekeeping_task x LEFT JOIN bus_service_request p ON p.id = x.service_request_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
